  "description": "Median house price divided by median annual household income \u2014 how many years of income it takes to buy a typical home. A ratio of 3x was historically considered affordable; above 5x is severely unaffordable.",
  "explainer": "In the 1980s, a typical Australian home cost around 3 times the annual median wage. Today it exceeds 10x nationally \u2014 meaning the average worker would need to save their entire income for a decade to buy the median home. No other chart better illustrates the generational wealth shift between those who bought before 2000 and those who didnt. Overlay with net migration, interest rates and housing approvals to see the full picture.",
